## Runtime and test environment

- The upstream launcher runs `statechart.ts` directly and needs Node 22.18 to 22.x, Node 23.6 or later, Bun 1.1.5 or later, or Deno 2.0 or later. jstack's own runtime needs Node 20.
- TLC is upstream's pin: `tla2tools.jar` 1.7.4 from https://github.com/tlaplus/tlaplus/releases/download/v1.7.4/tla2tools.jar, sha256 `936a262061c914694dfd669a543be24573c45d5aa0ff20a8b96b23d01e050e88`, with Java 11 or later.
- The upstream tests import `fast-check` 4.5.3. `tests/environment/` locks it; the contract runner installs that lock with `npm ci` only in a disposable snapshot and the owning suite links it into a temporary copy of the tests.
- The owning suite runs the upstream tests outside quick contracts with `JSTACK_STATECHART_NODE` (or the current Node when it can run TypeScript), `TLA2TOOLS` and `JAVA`, and fails when any of them is missing or any test is skipped. At the pinned commit, all 367 upstream tests passed on 2026-10-30 with Node 22.22.3, OpenJDK 17 and that jar.

